# Cómo citar el observatorio (Citation File Format). Los mismos créditos van dentro de cada fichero
# de datos publicado (configuracion/licencia_datos.json). / How to cite the observatory.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Si usas estos datos, cítalos así / If you use this data, please cite it as below:
  Alaniz Pintos, L. (2026). European Observatory of Drone Incidents. Versión / Version 2026-10.
  https://droneobservatory.eu. Licencia / Licence CC BY 4.0.
type: dataset
title: European Observatory of Drone Incidents
abbreviation: EODI
authors:
  - family-names: Alaniz Pintos
    given-names: Lucas
    name-suffix: PhD
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5179-2534"
    email: lucasalanizpintos@gmail.com
version: "2026-10"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://droneobservatory.eu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantuSync/droneobservatory"
repository-artifact: "https://droneobservatory.eu/datos/versiones/2026-10"
abstract: >-
  Public register of drone incidents in Europe, each with its sources and its level of
  confirmation, and of drone attacks on Ukraine according to official reports. The data
  (incidents, statuses, classifications and figures) are published under CC BY 4.0; the code is
  under Apache-2.0. Monthly citable versions: https://droneobservatory.eu/metodologia#versiones.
keywords:
  - drones
  - Europe
  - incidents
  - open data
